course: dictionary
lesson: 3112
title: Polite words for people
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «An elderly neighbour who lives alone may fall and need help, so tell a grown-up if you have not seen them for a while.» The clues are lives alone and may fall, so elderly describes an older person who may need help.
explain: Elderly is a polite word for old, used about people. You can also say «the elderly» to mean old people as a group, as in «care for the elderly». Try swapping in old: the sentence still makes sense, so elderly means old.
explain: Writers choose elderly because it sounds respectful. It tells the reader that the person is old and deserves care and kindness.
fact: Elderly is an adjective: «an elderly neighbour» means an old neighbour.
fact: «The elderly» is a noun phrase meaning old people as a group.
fact: Elderly people can be more at risk from falls, heat, cold and scams, so we look out for them.
fact: Kind ways to help elderly people include offering your seat, carrying bags, visiting and being patient.
fact: «Care for the elderly» means look after old people.
exercise: «An elderly neighbour who lives alone is cheered by being noticed.» What does elderly mean here? | *Old | Angry with everyone | Young and very fast | Lost in the town
exercise: Find and copy the word that is a polite word for old. | *elderly | tell | neighbour | bus
exercise: What is a good way to help an elderly neighbour? | Shout at them to hurry up | Ignore them if they are slow | *Offer to carry their bags | Tell them to go away
test: Ben says «the elderly» means young people. Why is he wrong? | Elderly means very fast | *The elderly means old people as a group | The elderly means children at school | The elderly means people who live in London
test: Why should you tell a grown-up if you have not seen an elderly neighbour for a while? | They may want a new car | Elderly people are always rude | Grown-ups like to know everything | *They may have fallen and need help
exam: Which sentence uses elderly with the right meaning? | The elderly car raced past the school | My elderly brother is ten years old | Elderly is the name of a fast dog | *Visit the elderly neighbour who lives alone and check she is warm
